# Quantumult X remote filter - Meta Muse (coverage-expanded)
# Updated: 2026-11-11
# Policy: Muse. Select ONE stable proxy node in the Muse policy group.
# Sources: Meta Muse transport teardown, public Muse routing reports,
# and Quantumult X/Facebook rules from community maintainers.
# Broad Meta/Facebook/Instagram suffixes are intentional: Muse authentication,
# assets, and live connections can be shared with those platforms.
# This ALSO routes unrelated Facebook/Instagram traffic via Muse.
# No MITM/rewrite/resource parser is required; avoid auto-switching nodes.
# Research note (2026-11-10): App transport domains (muse.ai, meta.ai,
# metaaivm.com, facebook.com) were already covered. Added adjacent Meta
# asset/link domains from community rule lists as a conservative fallback,
# NOT as proof they are needed by Muse. Do not add broad IP/ASN rules.
# Connection failures may also be Meta server/credential/region issues.
# In Quantumult X: refresh this remote resource; set force-policy=Muse,
# prefer inserted-resource=true for rule conflict; use a stable node.
# If it still fails, inspect Network Activity for unmatched/REJECT domains.

#
# 1. Muse site, AI APIs, dedicated cloud VMs and generated assets
host-suffix, muse.ai, Muse
host-suffix, metaaivm.com, Muse
host-suffix, meta.ai, Muse
host-suffix, metaaiusercontent.com, Muse
host-suffix, llama.com, Muse
host-suffix, atmeta.com, Muse
#
# 2. Shared Meta authentication, Graph APIs and service gateways
host-suffix, meta.com, Muse
host-suffix, facebook.com, Muse
host-suffix, facebook.net, Muse
host-suffix, fb.com, Muse
host-suffix, instagram.com, Muse
#
# 3. Shared Meta media/CDN/attachments
host-suffix, fbcdn.net, Muse
host-suffix, fbsbx.com, Muse
host-suffix, cdninstagram.com, Muse
host, fbcdn-a.akamaihd.net, Muse
#
#
# 2026-11-10 supplemental Meta CDN/short-link domains (possible shared assets)
# Source: blackmatrix7/ios_rule_script Facebook.list, NOT Muse packet capture
host-suffix, fbcdn.com, Muse
host-suffix, fbsbx.net, Muse
host-suffix, igcdn.com, Muse
host-suffix, fb.me, Muse
host-suffix, ig.me, Muse
#
# 4. Observed Muse endpoints (covered above but explicit for audit)
host, ai.meta.com, Muse
host, auth.meta.com, Muse
host, accountscenter.meta.com, Muse
host, meta.graph.meta.com, Muse
host, ar.graph.meta.com, Muse
host, hatch-api.meta.ai, Muse
host, api.meta.ai, Muse
host, agent.meta.ai, Muse
host, edge-metaclaw-http.c10r.facebook.com, Muse
host, shortwave.facebook.com, Muse
#
# 5. Additional Meta ecosystem fallbacks (community rules; NOT Muse-capture proof)
# Sources: MetaCubeX/meta-rules-dat geo/geosite/classical/meta.yaml
#          blackmatrix7/ios_rule_script rule/QuantumultX/Facebook/Facebook.list
# These are distinct Meta networking, deep-link and messaging endpoints missing
# from the 2026-11-10 Muse file. They may route unrelated Meta traffic.
# Deliberately exclude bulk WhatsApp/Threads domains, wide ASN/IP rules.
host-suffix, fbidb.io, Muse
host-suffix, fburl.com, Muse
host-suffix, tfbnw.net, Muse
host-suffix, fbmessenger.com, Muse
host-suffix, messenger.com, Muse
host-suffix, m.me, Muse
